  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Sunil Kumar vs The Managing Director Ksrtc on 3 April, 2024 Author: Pradeep Singh Yerur Bench: Pradeep Singh Yerur -1- NC: 2024:KHC:17008 MFA No. 969 of 2021 C/W MFA No. 5504 of 2021 IN THE HIGH COURT OF KARNATAKA AT BENGALURU DATED THIS THE 3RD DAY OF APRIL, 2024 BEFORE THE HON'BLE MR JUSTICE PRADEEP SINGH YERUR MISCELLANEOUS FIRST APPEAL NO.969 OF 2021 (MV-I) C/W MISCELLANEOUS FIRST APPEAL NO.5504 OF 2021 (MV-I) IN MFA NO.969/2021 BETWEEN: SUNIL KUMAR S/O NAGARAJU AGED ABOUT 25 YEARS, R/AT SANNAMALLEGOWDA BEEDI, WARD NO.17, PETE, MALAVALLI, MANDYA-571430. ...APPELLANT (BY SRI. RANGEGOWDA N.R., ADVOCATE) AND: THE MANAGING DIRECTOR KSRTC DEPOT BANGALORE CENTRAL OFFICE Digitally K H ROAD, SHANTHINAGAR, signed by B BENGALURU -560 027 LAVANYA ... RESPONDENT Location: (BY SMT. S.NIRMALA, ADVOCATE.) HIGH COURT OF KARNATAKA THIS MFA IS FILED U/S 173(1) OF MV ACT AGAINST THE JUDGMENT AND AWARD DATED 11.01.2021 PASSED IN MVC NO. 2910/2019 ON THE FILE OF THE VIII ADDITIONAL SMALL CAUSES JUDGE AND ACMM, MEMBER-MACT, BENGALURU (SCCH-5), PARTLY ALLOWING THE CLAIM PETITION FOR COMPENSATION AND SEEKING ENHANCEMENT OF COMPENSATION. -2- NC: 2024:KHC:17008 Sunil Kumar vs The Managing Director Ksrtc on 3 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/12472388/ 1 MFA No. 969 of 2021 C/W MFA No. 5504 of 2021 IN MFA NO.5504/2021 BETWEEN MANAGING DIRECTOR KSRTC, DEPOT BANGALORE CENTRAL OFFICE, K.H. ROAD, SHANTINAGAR, BANGALORE-27 REPRESENTED BY KARNATAKA STATE ROAD TRANSPORT CORPORATION CENTRAL OFFICE, BANGALORE, BY ITS CHIEF LAW OFFICER, BANGALORE ...APPELLANT (BY SMT.S. NIRMALA, ADVOCATE.) AND SUNIL KUMAR S/O NAGARAJU AGED 26 YEARS, R/O SANNAMALLEGOWDA BEEDI WARD NO.17, PETE MALAVALLI MANDYA DISTRICT. ... RESPONDENT (BY SRI. RANGEGOWDA N.R., ADVOCATE.) THIS MFA IS FILED U/S 173(1) OF MV ACT AGAINST THE JUDGMENT AND AWARD DATED 11.01.2021 PASSED IN MVC NO. 2910/2019 ON THE FILE OF THE VIII ADDITIONAL SCJ AND ACMM, MEMBER, MACT, BENGALURU SCCH-5, AWARDING COMPENSATION OF RS.8,77,000/- WITH INTEREST AT 9 PERCENT P.A. FROM THE DATE OF PETITION TILL REALIZATION. THESE APPEALS, COMING ON FOR FINAL HEARING, THIS DAY, THE COURT DELIVERED THE FOLLOWING: JUDGMENT",
    "facts": "The appeal preferred by the claimant is founded on the premise of inadequacy of compensation awarded and to [LEAKAGE_MASK] the contributory negligence of 10% fastened against the claimant whereas, the appeal preferred by the Corporation is on the ground of exorbitant compensation awarded and the entire negligence to be fastened on the rider of the motorcycle - claimant. Due to which, the claimant fell down and suffered grievous injuries. The claimant was aged 50 years as on the date of occurrence of accident. In view of the injuries suffered in the accident, the claimant filed a claim petition seeking compensation against Corporation. 3.2 On service of notice, the Corporation filed statement of objections denying the claim of the claimant including the age, avocation, income and the negligence NC: 2024:KHC:17008 attributed against the driver of the bus. Hence, sought for dismissal of the claim petition. On the basis of material evidence, both oral and documentary, the tribunal awarded the compensation of Rs.8,77,000/- by deducting Rs.77,000/- towards 10% of contributory negligence. The tribunal not agreeing with the degree of disability assessed by the Doctor, assessed disability of 20% to the whole body. However, the tribunal has assessed the disability at 20%, which is erroneous. However, the claimant was inpatient for 2 months. In view of the above, the claimant would be entitled to a total compensation of Rs.10,16,856/- as against Rs.8,77,000/- as mentioned in the table below: Heads Amount in Rs. Loss of future income 4,83,840-00 Pain and sufferings 1,00,000-00 Loss of amenities 25,000-00",
    "arguments": "Accordingly, he seeks enhancement of compensation. It is also contended that the entire negligence to be fastened as against the rider of the motorcycle - claimant and the tribunal has awarded higher compensation, which requires to be Sunil Kumar vs The Managing Director Ksrtc on 3 April, 2024 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/12472388/ 3 drastically reduced."
  },
